WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.159 --> 00:00:07.629
Do you make the same commitment that you will
absolutely- sir- that you will absolutely

00:00:07.629 --> 00:00:09.530
accept the result of this election.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:11.269
I will look at it at the time.

00:00:11.269 --> 00:00:12.330
It's rigged.

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:13.730
That's just not right.

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:21.039
I mean, this is a fair- first of all the election
is a state by state issue, so to think that

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:30.520
some sort of conspiracy exists that elections
can be rigged that's just- that's not good

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:33.900
for the system, when in fact it's not happening.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:40.030
During all the debates we had like four minutes
tonight spent on the deficit.

00:00:40.030 --> 00:00:42.440
For minutes out of all the debates!

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:47.020
And then there were really just a couple of
minutes spent on the entitlements, medicaid,

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:49.079
medicare, social security.

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:57.680
When these are really really huge issues and
not mentioned once were drugs.

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:04.379
Not mentioned once was the legalization of
marijuana and the fact that the number one

00:01:04.379 --> 00:01:10.390
category of arrest in this country in the
last year is marijuana related.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:14.600
That, that is flabbergasting and of course
completely missing.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:17.860
Yeah, economics was a big part of the last
part of the debate tonight,

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:19.240
what did you think about all that?

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:24.800
Well, Hillary, there's a certainty that Hillary
is going to raise taxes uh there is a certainty

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.440
when it comes to Trump that there is uncertainty.

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:35.250
I mean he's talking about economic growth,
well you can't count on economic growth you've

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.050
gotta actually cut government.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.130
That's the one thing you couldn't count on.

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:43.220
When he talks about restricting immigration
that's gonna have a negative impact on the

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:47.280
economy so, you know, I think Trump's toast.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.160
There are a lot of leaks from Wikileaks, emails
and the like, about the Clinton campaign.

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:53.120
What do you think about the leaks that have
happened so far?

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.250
You know I wish they would be receiving the
attention that they deserve.

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:04.200
But I'm afraid that Trump and his continued
foibles seem to take up the airwaves.

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.910
Look, when Hillary Clinton says one thing
in front of wall street and says another thing

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:11.440
in front of main street, that's hypocrisy.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.960
How's it feel to be watching the debates all-
all of the debates that have happened so far

00:02:15.970 --> 00:02:18.000
and not being up there yourself?

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:21.080
Well uh I am on the ballot in all 50 states

00:02:21.080 --> 00:02:24.460
so the only third party on the ballot in all 50 states.

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:31.110
I think that as a result of my campaign, the
Libertarian campaign this cycle, I think that

00:02:31.110 --> 00:02:37.090
could change in the future and it's because
of the showing that we, that we have, that

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:42.710
we've demonstrated and that it'll be reflected
probably next election cycle.

00:02:42.710 --> 00:02:50.020
If not still winning, I mean, all these revelations,
anything is possible and of course you have

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.799
no chance of winning if you're not in the
race.

